  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Maximus Federal Services obligated $430M in FY2026 to date. Maximus Federal Services received 47 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $9.1M, and obligations fell 71.0% year over year. Maximus Federal Services recorded larger annual totals in prior years: FY21 obligations were $1.4B, FY22 obligations were $1.1B, FY23 obligations were $1.1B, FY24 obligations were $1.1B, and FY25 obligations were $1.5B. Maximus Federal Services saw the Department of Health and Human Services and the Department of Education as the largest buying agencies in FY2026 to date with $229M and $143M respectively, followed by the Department of the Treasury at $42.2M. Maximus Federal Services concentrated its work in Computer Systems Design Services at $226M and Telemarketing Bureaus and Other Contact Centers at $129M, with additional activity in Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $73.2M. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Maximus Federal Services obligations this year?",
        "body": "Maximus Federal Services obligated $430M in FY2026 to date, with $229M from the Department of Health and Human Services and $143M from the Department of Education. Maximus Federal Services shows market concentration in Computer Systems Design Services at $226M and Telemarketing Bureaus and Other Contact Centers at $129M. Maximus Federal Services also recorded activity in Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $73.2M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 to date compare to prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "Maximus Federal Services obligated $430M in FY2026 to date compared with $1.5B in FY25 and $1.4B in FY21. Maximus Federal Services obligations were $1.1B in FY22, FY23, and FY24. Maximus Federal Services obligations fell 71.0% year over year."
      }
    ]
